WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.416 --> 00:00:32.125
After describing bodily austerity

2
00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:35.083
in the previous verses of Chapter 17,
Lord Krishna

3
00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:38.625
now, in this verse 17.15, explains
vangmaya tapa –

4
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:42.583
the austerity of speech.

5
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:45.083
Immense power lies within speech.

6
00:00:45.083 --> 00:00:47.125
It can do good

7
00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:50.208
or cause harm,

8
00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:54.291
connect relationships or break them,

9
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:56.208
lift one up

10
00:00:56.208 --> 00:00:59.083
or push one into downfall.

11
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:02.666
In both personal and spiritual life,

12
00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:06.333
speech is the mirror of our mind and heart.

13
00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:07.833
What is in the mind

14
00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.791
is what comes out through speech –

15
00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:12.375
this is why restraint of speech

16
00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:16.250
becomes a major means of self-purification.

17
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.625
In this verse Lord Krishna clarifies

18
00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:22.083
what sattvic speech should be like,

19
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:26.333
and with which qualities the austerity
of speech is considered complete.

20
00:01:31.125 --> 00:01:32.875
Lord Krishna says –

21
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:36.083
anudvegakaram vakyam! That is,

22
00:01:36.083 --> 00:01:39.333
speech that does not agitate anyone.

23
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:42.375
The first responsibility of disciplined speech

24
00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:45.416
is that it should not disturb others.

25
00:01:45.416 --> 00:01:48.083
This does not mean hiding the truth,

26
00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:50.375
but expressing it with sensitivity

27
00:01:50.375 --> 00:01:53.041
and respect.

28
00:01:53.041 --> 00:01:55.000
What matters is not only

29
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.750
what we say, but also

30
00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.833
how we say it.

31
00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:06.208
After this comes – satyam!
Speaking the truth is necessary,

32
00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:09.166
but it should be said at the right time, in the right way,

33
00:02:09.166 --> 00:02:12.750
and before the right person. 

34
00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.000
Otherwise, instead of healing or solving,

35
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.791
it can cause injury.

36
00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:22.416
Then comes – priyam.

37
00:02:22.416 --> 00:02:25.625
Words may be true but bitter,

38
00:02:25.625 --> 00:02:28.500
or sweet but untrue.

39
00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:34.875
Sattvic speech is that which is both
true and pleasant.

40
00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:38.041
The fourth quality is – hitam.

41
00:02:38.041 --> 00:02:42.500
Pleasant speech should not
become mere flattery,

42
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.708
but should carry the feeling of
guidance and well-being.

43
00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:49.666
Finally Lord Krishna says – svadhyaya-

44
00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:53.416
abhyasanam! That is, the regular

45
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:56.000
study and recitation of scriptures.

46
00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.208
Such speech keeps us connected
to higher truth.

47
00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:02.041
The study of scripture does not
only increase understanding,

48
00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:04.708
it also purifies the heart.

49
00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:06.375
In today's world, sarcasm

50
00:03:06.375 --> 00:03:09.458
and cleverness are taken to be intelligence.

51
00:03:09.458 --> 00:03:10.583
But when

52
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:13.666
cleverness is used to hurt others

53
00:03:13.666 --> 00:03:16.750
or to mock them,

54
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.666
then it is a misuse of intellect.

55
00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:23.250
True cleverness is only that
which brings people closer –

56
00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:27.333
to us, to truth, and to the Paramatma.

57
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:30.541
Trying to correct someone without
building a relationship is futile.

58
00:03:30.541 --> 00:03:32.833
Words spoken with trust

59
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:34.625
settle into the heart,

60
00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:38.375
words spoken without trust bounce back

61
00:03:38.375 --> 00:03:42.375
after colliding, or fill the mind with bitterness.

62
00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.916
When practised with awareness,

63
00:03:44.916 --> 00:03:46.250
speech itself becomes

64
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.833
of transformation in one's own life and

65
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:52.166
in the lives of others – a powerful means.

66
00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.541
You speak carefully with others –

67
00:04:00.541 --> 00:04:06.333
but how do you speak with yourself?

68
00:04:06.333 --> 00:04:08.375
Are your inner words

69
00:04:08.375 --> 00:04:11.291
filled with criticism, blame,

70
00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:14.041
or constant pressure?

71
00:04:14.041 --> 00:04:18.958
I want you to know –

72
00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.166
vangmaya tapasya,

73
00:04:22.166 --> 00:04:26.250
that is, the austerity of speech –

74
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:31.041
begins with how you speak to yourself.

75
00:04:31.041 --> 00:04:33.416
The voice of your mind

76
00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:38.083
should not be your harshest enemy.

77
00:04:38.083 --> 00:04:43.833
Speak to yourself without agitation –

78
00:04:43.833 --> 00:04:47.541
anu-dvegakaram.

79
00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:49.041
Speak the truth –

80
00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:53.083
satyam – but not harshly.

81
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:55.958
Make your words

82
00:04:55.958 --> 00:04:58.208
priyam –

83
00:04:58.208 --> 00:05:00.500
kind and affectionate –

84
00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:07.750
even when you are correcting your own mistake.

85
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.000
Ask yourself –

86
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.958
‘Is what I am saying hitam?

87
00:05:14.958 --> 00:05:19.000
That is, is it helpful, or only harmful?’

88
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.416
Just as you recite the sacred scriptures,

89
00:05:23.416 --> 00:05:29.000
in the same way make your
self-talk sacred too.

90
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.416
Remind yourself

91
00:05:30.416 --> 00:05:33.666
of those truths

92
00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:36.291
that lift you higher,

93
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:38.250
not those that pull you down.

94
00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:41.583
A mind that is watered with kind

95
00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:44.750
and truthful words

96
00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:48.916
becomes fertile for growth.

97
00:05:48.916 --> 00:05:53.791
Transform your inner dialogue,

98
00:05:53.791 --> 00:05:55.416
and you will see

99
00:05:55.416 --> 00:05:59.375
that your outer life too begins to change.

100
00:05:59.375 --> 00:06:05.000
The discipline of speech is not
 only for the tongue –

101
00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.708
it is for the heart too.

102
00:06:11.541 --> 00:06:14.500
In your family, every word

103
00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:19.541
you speak has weight.

104
00:06:19.541 --> 00:06:23.000
You may not see it in the moment, but

105
00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.166
your speech can build a bridge,

106
00:06:27.166 --> 00:06:28.791
and can also build a wall.

107
00:06:28.791 --> 00:06:31.500
Always speak with awareness,

108
00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.958
especially with those

109
00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:37.166
who are closest to you.

110
00:06:37.166 --> 00:06:40.875
Satyam – that is, truth – is important!

111
00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:43.000
But without kindness, the spoken

112
00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.166
truth can cause a wound.

113
00:06:46.166 --> 00:06:50.833
So make your words gentle.

114
00:06:50.833 --> 00:06:53.041
Anudvegakaram –

115
00:06:53.041 --> 00:06:58.041
such that they do not agitate or hurt anyone.

116
00:06:58.041 --> 00:07:01.541
Let the words be priyam –
pleasant, not sarcastic

117
00:07:01.541 --> 00:07:04.916
or disrespectful.

118
00:07:04.916 --> 00:07:09.500
Speak only what is hitam – truly beneficial,

119
00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:12.791
not merely an emotional reaction.

120
00:07:12.791 --> 00:07:14.041
And from time to time,

121
00:07:14.041 --> 00:07:17.833
share words of scripture and knowledge –

122
00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:21.666
svadhyaya-abhyasanam –

123
00:07:21.666 --> 00:07:25.333
so that the atmosphere of the
family rises higher.

124
00:07:25.333 --> 00:07:27.583
If children do not get very good

125
00:07:27.583 --> 00:07:30.666
results in an exam,

126
00:07:30.666 --> 00:07:32.750
then scolding them or mocking

127
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:35.750
them will not do them any good.

128
00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:39.750
But by supporting them with sympathy,

129
00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:42.250
you will surely get from them

130
00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:44.750
a better exam result next time!

131
00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.541
Your loved ones

132
00:07:46.541 --> 00:07:51.208
do not only remember what you said;

133
00:07:51.208 --> 00:07:54.458
they also treasure in their memories

134
00:07:54.458 --> 00:07:58.833
how you made them feel.

135
00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:01.666
A kind sentence spoken at the right time

136
00:08:01.666 --> 00:08:05.000
can open the window of someone's heart,

137
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.750
while a harsh word

138
00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:10.166
can keep it closed for years.

139
00:08:10.166 --> 00:08:13.083
Do not only live with your family –

140
00:08:13.083 --> 00:08:16.500
connect with them too. And for this,

141
00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.875
your words are the key.

142
00:08:19.875 --> 00:08:21.958
Speak as if

143
00:08:21.958 --> 00:08:23.708
the measure of your love

144
00:08:23.708 --> 00:08:27.416
depends on those very words –

145
00:08:27.416 --> 00:08:29.416
because very often,

146
00:08:29.416 --> 00:08:30.875
this is the truth.

147
00:08:35.666 --> 00:08:39.166
At the workplace, your words often have

148
00:08:39.166 --> 00:08:41.208
more power

149
00:08:41.208 --> 00:08:45.166
than you can even imagine – especially

150
00:08:45.166 --> 00:08:49.250
when you are in a position to correct, to guide,

151
00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.250
or to lead.

152
00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.000
I want to remind you –

153
00:08:56.000 --> 00:08:58.833
feedback is not only for being right,

154
00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:02.125
but also for being effective.

155
00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:06.083
Let your speech be anudvegakaram –

156
00:09:06.083 --> 00:09:09.500
such that it does not disturb anyone.

157
00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.791
Even while speaking about mistakes,
do not awaken fear

158
00:09:12.791 --> 00:09:16.208
or defensiveness in anyone.

159
00:09:16.208 --> 00:09:18.583
Let your speech be satyam –

160
00:09:18.583 --> 00:09:21.500
true – but not harsh.

161
00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:26.000
Let it be priyam – pleasant – but not sarcastic.

162
00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.333
Let it be hitam –

163
00:09:27.333 --> 00:09:30.958
truly helpful, not a hidden punishment.

164
00:09:30.958 --> 00:09:33.125
And whenever possible,

165
00:09:33.125 --> 00:09:38.291
connect your communication with
deeper values –

166
00:09:38.291 --> 00:09:41.500
svadhyaya-abhyasanam –

167
00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.958
reminding the team not only ‘what to do,’

168
00:09:44.958 --> 00:09:49.041
but also ‘why to do it.’

169
00:09:49.041 --> 00:09:50.625
True leadership

170
00:09:50.625 --> 00:09:53.833
refines speech to such a level

171
00:09:53.833 --> 00:09:56.625
that it guides,

172
00:09:56.625 --> 00:09:58.875
but does not injure;

173
00:09:58.875 --> 00:10:02.166
corrects, but does not crush.

174
00:10:02.166 --> 00:10:06.750
The words that awaken enthusiasm and respect

175
00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.958
are the ones remembered for a long time;

176
00:10:09.958 --> 00:10:12.375
words that give insult

177
00:10:12.375 --> 00:10:15.458
are not forgotten quickly,

178
00:10:15.458 --> 00:10:17.833
but leave wounds behind.

179
00:10:17.833 --> 00:10:20.416
Scolding an employee

180
00:10:20.416 --> 00:10:21.708
publicly for a mistake

181
00:10:21.708 --> 00:10:25.500
only increases their distress.

182
00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.208
But by speaking calmly in private,

183
00:10:28.208 --> 00:10:32.208
their way of working can be improved.

184
00:10:32.208 --> 00:10:35.875
Similarly, if there is a complaint
with management,

185
00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:40.291
then instead of directly making
an agitated display,

186
00:10:40.291 --> 00:10:44.625
a better solution comes from presenting
your point with humility.

187
00:10:44.625 --> 00:10:47.500
When your speech is sattvic,

188
00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:52.625
then your leadership becomes transformative –

189
00:10:52.625 --> 00:10:54.708
this happens not through your loud voice,

190
00:10:54.708 --> 00:10:56.125
but through your

191
00:10:56.125 --> 00:11:00.375
being listened to seriously.

192
00:11:00.375 --> 00:11:02.916
Speak with purpose –

193
00:11:02.916 --> 00:11:04.208
your leadership will

194
00:11:04.208 --> 00:11:08.500
surely leave a lasting impact.

195
00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:09.458
Reflect on this.
